  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "For this question, use the identity $\\cos 2\\theta=1-2\\sin^{2}\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $s=\\sin15^{\\circ}$. Show that $s=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$s=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}{2}$.",
          "worked": "Let $\\theta=15^{\\circ}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos30^{\\circ}&=1-2\\sin^{2}15^{\\circ}\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&=1-2s^{2}\\\\2s^{2}&=1-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\2s^{2}&=\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\s^{2}&=\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{4}\\\\s&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nTake the positive root because $\\sin15^{\\circ}>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Expand and simplify $\\dfrac{(\\sqrt3-1)^{2}}{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2-\\sqrt3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^{2}}{2}&=\\frac{3-2\\sqrt3+1}{2}\\\\\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^{2}}{2}&=2-\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that $\\sin15^{\\circ}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin15^{\\circ}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}$.",
          "worked": "Using parts a and b,\n$$\\begin{align*}s^{2}&=\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{4}\\\\s^{2}&=\\frac{\\dfrac{(\\sqrt3-1)^{2}}{2}}{4}\\\\s^{2}&=\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^{2}}{8}\\\\s&=\\frac{\\sqrt3-1}{\\sqrt8}\\\\s&=\\frac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $s=\\sin15^{\\circ}>0$ and $\\sqrt3-1>0$, take the positive root. Thus $\\sin15^{\\circ}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
